rem Odd Triplets
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=242
rem Count the triples (n, k, f) that are
rem all odd, with n up to Limit, f being
rem the number of k-subsets of 1 to n
rem with an odd sum

use bits
use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 1000000000000

rem The triples are exactly n = 4 a + 1
rem and k = 2 b + 1 with C(2 a, b) odd.
rem By Lucas that holds when the bits of
rem b are among those of 2 a, which is
rem 2^pop(a) choices of b. So the count
rem is the sum of 2^pop(a) for a below
rem M = (Limit - 1) // 4 + 1. Each set
rem bit i of M adds 3^i times 2^c for c
rem the set bits above it.
M = (Limit - 1) // 4 + 1
I = 0 to ((M binary len) - 1) array
Bit = (M bit I) choose 1 0
Above' = (Bit sum) - (Bit scan +)
Share' = Bit * 2 ** Above * 3 ** I
Answer = Share sum
Answer print
